==Strategy==	
This stage features Cafeteria Cat supported by J.J. Jackrabbit and Mr. Mole. The latter two's [[Knockback]] combined with Cafeteria Cat's low range and speed can cause your Cats to lose ground easily. Most tanks will be ineffective because of the aforementioned Knockback, but also Cafeteria Cat's high damage.

Luring Cafeteria Cat near your base to avoid dealing with the Mr. Mole for a while can be a good strategy to get in some damage.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]]: Stone is immune to Knockback and won't be killed by Cafeteria Cat's attacks, making them a great choice for maintaining ground. Using Research Combos to decrease the amount of time between Stone Cats is highly recommended.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]: Courier is a staple in any stage with Red enemies, and can kill the J.J. Jackrabbits and Sir Seals easily. Beware that they don't outrange Cafeteria Cat's [[Omni Strike]].
*[[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Lord of Ruin Jagando Jr.]]: Has great stats against Traitless, and is immune to Curse in case Cafeteria Cat manages to land a hit on him. The Mr. Mole can cause problems for him though.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[EPICFEST (Gacha Event)|EPICFEST]] Units: EPICFEST units are an obvious choice for a stage where the main threat is Traitless. Some good examples are [[Kasli the Bane (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasli the Bane]], who has high DPS and can Curse both Cafeteria Cat and the peons, allowing the use of more anti-Traitless units, and [[D'arktanyan (Uber Rare Cat)|D'arktanyan]], who has exceptionally high DPS against Traitless.

